Scenarios:
1. How Partition works with consumer groups
2. Offset Commit Setting
3. When a consumer fails

1. How Partition and Consumer group work together
Rule: One Partition -> One consumer(per group)
Partitions: P0, P1, P2
Consumers: C1, C2, C3

Assignment:
P0 - C1
P1 - C2
P2 - C3

Important scenarios
Case1: Equal consumers and Partitions
- Perfect balance, maximum parallelism

Case2: More consumers than partition
Partitions: P0, P1
Consumers: C1, C2, C3
One consumer will be idle

Case3: More partitions than consumers
Partitions: P0, P1, P3
Consumers: C1, C2
In this case consumer may handle multiple partitions

When if any consumer fails:
Before:
- P0 -> C1, P1 -> C2 then 
C1 crashes

After rebalance
P0 -> C2
P1 -> C2
No data loss

------------------------
2. Offset Commit Setting

a) Auto Commit
spring.kafka.consumer.enale-auto-commit=true
- kafka commits offset automatically
- Risk: message may be marked "read" before processing finishes so there is risk of data loss.

b) Manual Commit (Recommended)
spring.kafka.consumer.enale-auto-commit=false

Then in code
    @KafkaListener(topics = "my-topic", groupId="my-group")
    public void consume(String message) {
        System.out.println("Received: " + message);
	process(message);    
	ack.acknowledge();
}

This is safe as the message is marked done only after success.
----------------------------------------------------------
3. When a consumer fails
Lets say consumer C1 fails after reading 3 messages and before 4th message.
When it is up it joins the consumer group.
Consumer notifies kafka that I am part of group X, give me my assignment.
Then Kafka responds with:
Kafka sends:
 1. Assigned partitions: (e.g. P0)
 2. Last committed message offset (e.g. 3)

Now consumer starts polling 
consumer.poll()
this means "Give me message starting from offset 3"
Then Kafka responds with M4, M5,... 

Full Flow:
1. Consumer joins group
2. Kafka assigns partitions + offset =3
3. Consumer -> poll()
4. Kafka -> return messages from offset 3 (M4)
5. Consumer processes M4
6. Consumer commits offset = 4

